### Do not fail the detector test when its hotkey is unavailable

If another process already owns Ctrl+Alt+Shift+F24, `RegisterHotKey` fails and this assertion makes the test fail before conflict detection is exercised. Please treat unavailable registration as an unmet test precondition: log the reason and return without running the assertions. When registration succeeds, retain the existing scope-exit cleanup and System-conflict checks.

```suggestion
            if (!RegisterHotKey(nullptr, testHotkeyId, MOD_CONTROL | MOD_ALT | MOD_SHIFT, VK_F24))
            {
                Logger::WriteMessage(L"Skipping system-conflict check: Ctrl+Alt+Shift+F24 is unavailable.");
                return;
            }
```
